KZ3 patch 1063 (SPU pass 48): the PS3_SAMPLE sampler thread must not take the loader lock while it holds
another thread suspended. samp_mod_hit (GetModuleHandleExA + GetModuleFileNameA) and samp_rva_hit's first
GetModuleHandleA ran between SuspendThread and ResumeThread; under Wine those enter the loader critical section
(LdrFindEntryForAddress), so a thread suspended inside LoadLibrary / a DLL entry / any Ldr* path was never resumed
and the game froze: KZ3 spu-48q1 (level freeze at 124 s, sampler reports and the main thread stop together) and
the coordinator's quit-dbg (7 flips, early boot). The module attribution now runs after ResumeThread; only the
context read, the lock-free sorted-map lookup and the stack read (NtReadVirtualMemory) stay inside the window.
Upstream candidate (general toolkit bug; every sampled run can hit it).

diff --git a/runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp b/runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp
--- a/runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp
+++ b/runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp
@@ -660,18 +660,29 @@
                                       FALSE, te.th32ThreadID);
                 if (!h) continue;
                 if (SuspendThread(h) != (DWORD)-1) {
+                    /* KZ3 patch 1063: while the thread is suspended do only lock-free work (its context,
+                     * the sorted-map lookup, the stack read). GetModuleHandleEx / GetModuleFileName
+                     * (samp_mod_hit) and GetModuleHandle (samp_rva_hit) take the loader lock; a thread
+                     * suspended while holding it (Wine's LdrFindEntryForAddress, LoadLibrary, DLL init) was
+                     * never resumed: the sampler blocked on the lock and the game froze with it (KZ3
+                     * spu-48q1: level freeze at 124 s, the sampler's reports stop at the same moment; the
+                     * coordinator's quit-dbg: 7 flips). The module attribution runs after ResumeThread. */
                     CONTEXT c; c.ContextFlags = CONTEXT_CONTROL;
-                    if (GetThreadContext(h, &c)) {
-                        s_samp_total++;
-                        uint32_t g = samp_lookup((uintptr_t)c.Rip);
+                    int got = GetThreadContext(h, &c);
+                    uint32_t g = 0;
+                    if (got) {
+                        g = samp_lookup((uintptr_t)c.Rip);
                         if (!g && s_samp_main > 0) g = samp_stack_guest(h, &c);
+                    }
+                    ResumeThread(h);
+                    if (got) {
+                        s_samp_total++;
                         if (g) { s_samp_guest++; samp_hit(g); samp_tid_hit(te.th32ThreadID);
                                  samp_tid2(te.th32ThreadID, 1, 0); }
                         else { int nt = samp_mod_hit((uintptr_t)c.Rip);
                                if (!nt) samp_rva_hit((uintptr_t)c.Rip);
                                samp_tid2(te.th32ThreadID, 0, nt); }
                     }
-                    ResumeThread(h);
                 }
                 CloseHandle(h);
             } while (Thread32Next(snap, &te));
